WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.310 --> 00:00:05.080
Despite performing poorly upon release both
critically and commercially, 1995's Empire

00:00:05.080 --> 00:00:09.470
Records has gone on to become a coming-of-age
classic, gradually amassing a cult following

00:00:09.470 --> 00:00:10.660
in the decades since.

00:00:10.660 --> 00:00:14.380
For some of the cast members, Empire Records
was a launching pad for long and fruitful

00:00:14.380 --> 00:00:15.380
careers.

00:00:15.380 --> 00:00:18.140
For others, the beloved teen flick wound up
being their pinnacle.

00:00:18.140 --> 00:00:21.190
Here's what the cast of Empire Records looks
like today.

00:00:21.190 --> 00:00:22.730
Liv Tyler - Corey

00:00:22.730 --> 00:00:26.560
After her rock star dad Steven Tyler cast
her in the music video for Aerosmith's hit

00:00:26.560 --> 00:00:31.369
song "Crazy," Liv Tyler landed her first major
movie role as overachieving student Corey

00:00:31.369 --> 00:00:32.660
in Empire Records.

00:00:32.660 --> 00:00:36.590
Co-star Maxwell Caulfield later admitted that
the male cast members found it hard to keep

00:00:36.590 --> 00:00:40.500
their eyes off this "emerging swan," prompting
Tyler's mother to remain on set so she should

00:00:40.500 --> 00:00:42.670
could keep her daughter's admirers in check.

00:00:42.670 --> 00:00:46.860
Since then, Tyler gained worldwide fame playing
Elf maiden Arwen in Peter Jackson's The Lord

00:00:46.860 --> 00:00:48.050
of the Rings trilogy.

00:00:48.050 --> 00:00:51.250
More recently she's starred as a regular on
the HBO series The Leftovers.

00:00:51.250 --> 00:00:55.620
And she's moved into producing, pulling the
strings on the fantasy horror project Wildling,

00:00:55.620 --> 00:00:59.290
which stars Tyler opposite Bel Powley and
Brad Dourif.

00:00:59.290 --> 00:01:00.790
Coyote Shivers - Berko

00:01:00.790 --> 00:01:05.089
While it's true that Liv Tyler's mother Bebe
Buell provided a chaperone service for her

00:01:05.089 --> 00:01:08.220
daughter on set, there was actually a second
reason for her being there.

00:01:08.220 --> 00:01:13.450
Buell married Berko actor Francis "Coyote"
Shivers in 1992, meaning that Tyler was acting

00:01:13.450 --> 00:01:17.500
alongside her 24-year-old step-dad in Empire
Records with her mother watching over them

00:01:17.500 --> 00:01:18.500
both.

00:01:18.500 --> 00:01:19.500
Cool.

00:01:19.500 --> 00:01:23.869
Shivers and Buell divorced in 1999 and he
has since worked as a musician and DJ in the

00:01:23.869 --> 00:01:28.200
Los Angeles area, though his club work was
put on hold in September 2015 — when he

00:01:28.200 --> 00:01:32.170
started a nine month prison sentence for violating
the terms of a restraining order filed against

00:01:32.170 --> 00:01:34.220
him by his second wife, Pauley Perrette.

00:01:34.220 --> 00:01:36.600
Renée Zellweger - Gina

00:01:36.600 --> 00:01:41.710
After making her debut opposite fellow unknown
Matthew McConaughey in the 1994 flop Texas

00:01:41.710 --> 00:01:45.689
Chainsaw Massacre: The Next Generation, Renee
Zellweger rebounded with a breakthrough role

00:01:45.689 --> 00:01:47.689
as Gina in Empire Records.

00:01:47.689 --> 00:01:51.670
She ended up riding that buzz to superstardom
in Jerry Maguire, and later won an Academy

00:01:51.670 --> 00:01:54.770
Award for her performance in 2003's Cold Mountain.

00:01:54.770 --> 00:01:58.590
Of course, everyone knows what Zellweger looks
like these days, because of an ongoing tabloid

00:01:58.590 --> 00:02:02.119
controversy over whether or not she's had
plastic surgery to change her looks.

00:02:02.119 --> 00:02:06.049
Zellweger has risen above the nonsense and
continues to perform in films like Bridget

00:02:06.049 --> 00:02:08.819
Jones' Baby and Same Kind of Different as
Me.

00:02:08.819 --> 00:02:10.970
Rory Cochrane - Lucas

00:02:10.970 --> 00:02:15.099
Few young actors were as ubiquitous in the
'90s as Rory Cochrane, who appeared in ten

00:02:15.099 --> 00:02:18.810
films that decade, including Dogtown and Dazed
&amp; Confused, in addition to Empire Records.

00:02:18.810 --> 00:02:23.750
These days he's best known for starring in
50 episodes of CSI: Miami as Timothy Speedle,

00:02:23.750 --> 00:02:27.340
though he continues to appear on the big screen
as a character actor in films like Argo and

00:02:27.340 --> 00:02:28.909
Black Mass.

00:02:28.909 --> 00:02:30.659
Robin Tunney - Debra

00:02:30.659 --> 00:02:34.269
With her shaved head, Robin Tunney caught
the attention of Hollywood as suicidal teen

00:02:34.269 --> 00:02:35.980
Debra in Empire Records.

00:02:35.980 --> 00:02:39.750
That led to roles in a string of big budget
blockbusters, but the gravy train derailed

00:02:39.750 --> 00:02:42.340
when 2000's Supernova became a super flop.

00:02:42.340 --> 00:02:45.739
Though she's continued to appear in minor
films since, Tunney has found more success

00:02:45.739 --> 00:02:51.129
on the small screen, appearing in over 150
episodes of The Mentalist as Teresa Lisbon.

00:02:51.129 --> 00:02:52.959
Ethan Embry - Mark

00:02:52.959 --> 00:02:57.040
The definition of a working actor, Ethan Embry
has appeared in film and on television every

00:02:57.040 --> 00:03:01.400
single year since Empire Records came out
in 1995 — even if you may not remember any

00:03:01.400 --> 00:03:02.530
of those appearances.

00:03:02.530 --> 00:03:06.670
While his most famous role is probably as
Rusty Griswold in Vegas Vacation, Embry is

00:03:06.670 --> 00:03:10.900
still going strong with guest spots on shows
like The Walking Dead and Once Upon a Time.

00:03:10.900 --> 00:03:13.790
Pretty good work if you don't mind getting
literally eaten alive.

00:03:13.790 --> 00:03:15.629
Johnny Whitworth - AJ

00:03:15.629 --> 00:03:19.280
Though he's best known for his role as AJ
in Empire Records, Johnny Whitworth almost

00:03:19.280 --> 00:03:22.540
played a totally different character — he
initially wanted to play the part of Lucas

00:03:22.540 --> 00:03:23.540
instead.

00:03:23.540 --> 00:03:27.459
He told Starry Mag "I wanted to be Lucas because
he had great one-liners, but he didn't get

00:03:27.459 --> 00:03:29.280
to kiss Liv Tyler at the end!

00:03:29.280 --> 00:03:30.681
Everything comes together as God intends it."

00:03:30.681 --> 00:03:32.530
"You're so special and you're so talented
and you've everything it takes you have more

00:03:32.530 --> 00:03:38.579
than everything it takes and you're really
stupid because you don't know that."

00:03:39.579 --> 00:03:42.430
Since then, the almighty has apparently intended
Whitworth to become a TV star, as he's had

00:03:42.430 --> 00:03:46.299
recurring roles on CSI: Miami, The 100, and
Blindspot.

00:03:46.299 --> 00:03:48.049
Anthony LaPaglia - Joe

00:03:48.049 --> 00:03:52.060
Australian actor Anthony LaPaglia was a late
bloomer as a thespian, moving to New York

00:03:52.060 --> 00:03:54.909
City in his early twenties in the hope of
one day becoming an actor.

00:03:54.909 --> 00:03:58.930
By the late '80s he was regularly landing
gigs, eventually leading to his role as Joe

00:03:58.930 --> 00:04:00.280
in Empire Records.

00:04:00.280 --> 00:04:04.450
Since then, he's become most famous for his
Golden Globe-winning turn as suicidal FBI

00:04:04.450 --> 00:04:07.909
agent Jack Malone in the CBS drama Without
A Trace.

00:04:07.909 --> 00:04:08.940
"Superb."

00:04:10.320 --> 00:04:12.040
"Say it again."

00:04:12.040 --> 00:04:13.079
"Superb."

00:04:13.079 --> 00:04:15.260
Maxwell Caulfield - Rex Manning

00:04:15.260 --> 00:04:19.500
Washed up musician Rex Manning was the butt
of the joke in Empire Records, but actor Maxwell

00:04:19.500 --> 00:04:21.209
Caulfield is anything but washed-up.

00:04:21.209 --> 00:04:24.280
Though some may know him best for his role
as Manning, Caulfield has actually appeared

00:04:24.280 --> 00:04:28.640
in nearly 40 feature films, while also working
on stage and providing voices for audiobooks,

00:04:28.640 --> 00:04:30.240
cartoons, and video games.

00:04:30.280 --> 00:04:31.240
Say no more.

00:04:31.240 --> 00:04:33.560
"And you were my favorite singer in high school."

00:04:34.800 --> 00:04:37.720
"Who's your favorite singer now?"

00:04:37.720 --> 00:04:38.680
"You!

00:04:38.690 --> 00:04:39.690
It's still you!"

00:04:39.690 --> 00:04:41.289
Debi Mazar - Jane

00:04:41.289 --> 00:04:45.310
Empire Records is just one many major motion
pictures where you may have seen Debi Mazar.

00:04:45.310 --> 00:04:49.139
She's also appeared in films like Goodfellas,
Malcolm X, and Batman Forever.

00:04:49.139 --> 00:04:52.710
She's since gone on to star in television
as well, with a recurring role as publicist

00:04:52.710 --> 00:04:54.380
Shauna in Entourage.

00:04:54.380 --> 00:04:57.850
If that weren't enough, she and her husband
Gabriele Corcos have their own show on the

00:04:57.850 --> 00:04:59.180
Cooking Channel.

00:04:59.180 --> 00:05:00.990
Brendan Sexton - Warren

00:05:00.990 --> 00:05:05.389
Before playing Warren in Empire Records, Brendan
Sexton had already earned an Independent Spirit

00:05:05.389 --> 00:05:08.220
Awards nomination for his role in Welcome
to the Dollhouse.

00:05:08.220 --> 00:05:11.500
That was pretty much the highlight of his
career, though he continues to appear as a

00:05:11.500 --> 00:05:16.210
character actor in ensembles like Black Hawk
Down, which he later publicly criticized for

00:05:16.210 --> 00:05:18.440
the film's portrayal of Somalis.

00:05:18.440 --> 00:05:20.319
James 'Kimo' Wills - Eddie

00:05:20.319 --> 00:05:22.520
Not everyone is cut out to be a superstar.

00:05:22.520 --> 00:05:26.300
Kimo Wills is one of those folks, as the guy
who played Eddie has since pretty much dropped

00:05:26.300 --> 00:05:30.750
out of acting altogether after a string of
appearances as extras and other minor characters.

00:05:30.750 --> 00:05:34.640
These days, he's just a normal dude doing
things like playing video games, reading comics,

00:05:34.640 --> 00:05:36.470
and retweeting cute dog photos.

00:05:36.470 --> 00:05:38.620
Hey, the world needs regular folks too!

00:05:38.620 --> 00:05:39.620
Thanks for watching!

00:05:39.620 --> 00:05:41.660
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:05:41.660 --> 00:05:43.820
Plus check out all this cool stuff we know
you'll love, too!

